rhythm echo consent verify: check an evidence folder's hashes and signature

Usage:
  rhythm echo consent verify <folder|file> [--key <file>]

Flags:
      --json                 write JSON to stdout
  -q, --quiet                only the verdict and what failed
      --plain                no color or glyphs (screen readers, logs)
      --no-color             no color
      --key <file>           the ed25519 public key (PEM) to check
                             consent.json.sig with

Exit codes: 0 every file and the signature match, 1 a hash or the signature
doesn't match, 2 usage error, 3 a file is missing or unreadable.
rhythm echo consent --help lists the consent check's flags.
rhythm echo help lists every command.
